From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: verisilicon: Allow cache hints on a decoder's capture queue

A CPU that reads decoded pictures, to convert, scale or hash them,
reads them uncached: dma-contig allocates the capture queue coherent.
Let userspace ask a decoder for non-coherent buffers with
V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT; videobuf2 then syncs them for the CPU
when they are dequeued and for the device when they are queued. An
encoder's capture queue holds the bitstream, which the kernel fills in
for JPEG, and keeps its coherent buffers.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_drv.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_drv.c b/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_drv.c
index 3202146..00f30f8 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_drv.c
@@ -239,6 +239,7 @@ queue_init(void *priv, struct vb2_queue *src_vq, struct vb2_queue *dst_vq)
 	if (!ctx->is_encoder) {
 		dst_vq->dma_attrs |= DMA_ATTR_NO_KERNEL_MAPPING;
 		dst_vq->max_num_buffers = MAX_POSTPROC_BUFFERS;
+		dst_vq->allow_cache_hints = 1;
 	}
 
 	dst_vq->type = V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE;
